I'm 99.99999999% sure that the sudden flip observation is not related to any change to AVPro, because VRChat has not upgraded from 2.8.5 for.... many years at this point. There have been previous requests to update AVPro, but there are technical limitations in the AVPro 3.x versions for VRChat that prevented it at the time they reviewed the concern. Would be good if VRChat could allocate another review of an AVPro version upgrade, it's sorely needed.

As for UNITY_UV_STARTS_AT_TOP, this is an implicit macro that Unity itself sets via the engine internals. It's not something VRChat could or even would want to try messing with (too much effort, not enough gained).

For now, just do like everyone else does and pass in a bool into the material to flip the texture. You can check for quest vs PC by using C# compile directives, then passing that bool into you shader/material.

#if UNITY_ANDROID // Quest is an android build

bool isAndroid = true;

bool isIOS = false;

#elif UNITY_IOS

bool isAndroid = false;

bool isIOS = true;

#else

bool isAndroid = false;

bool isIOS = false;

#endif

(more platform defines here https://docs.unity3d.com/2022.2/Documentation/Manual/PlatformDependentCompilation.html , note that VRChat only uses Android/iOS/WindowsStandalone defines).
